Category: libycxx-limitation. The test case "terminate_on_exception: enabled" installs a
terminate handler with std::set_terminate in the test program and expects libtbb.so's call of
std::terminate to reach it, which needs one C++ runtime shared by the program and libtbb.so; the
test already leaves itself out for MSVC's statically linked runtime ("The test cannot work
correctly with statically linked runtime"). Each image that links libycxx has its own ABI runtime
and terminate handler (DECISIONS §2; STATUS, known limitations): the guard also requires a
shared runtime (libstdc++, libc++ or MSVC's).

diff --git a/test/conformance/conformance_global_control.cpp b/test/conformance/conformance_global_control.cpp
